{"what":"House bodies behind the survey's open street fronts, read from the satellite image (Aras 13 Nov 2026 05:14 UTC: 'Look at settalite imagery for those'). Survey m, one closed ring each (no holes).","source":"Esri World Imagery, Maxar capture of 1 Mar 2023, 0.31 m source, used at 0.5 m in survey coordinates (library/satellite_2026-11-06/sat_2023-03-01_0p5m_survey.jpg); fronts from the Basemap cache of 13 Nov 2026 (Basemap v9.4 run).","method":"Roofs by colour rules (tile: R-B>55, R>G+22, R>105; bright sheet: max>175, saturation<0.17; blue sheet: B>R+18, B>120), cleaned, patches under 15 m2 dropped. Image moved onto the survey per 200 m tile by best overlap with closed survey buildings (overall 2 m east, 4 m north). For every survey building line that closes no outline and is 2 m or longer (party-wall ticks under 3 m left out), cut in pieces of about 9 m: rays every 1 m to both sides, depth = where the roof ends (2.5 m of no roof), stopped at closed survey buildings, at used OpenStreetMap footprints, at another open front beyond 4.5 m, and at 22 m. The side with more roof is taken (party-wall ticks add weight); a piece gets a body when 40 % of its rays find 3.5 m of roof or more; body = the front moved back by the median depth. Bodies joined, closed survey buildings and used OSM footprints cut away, parts under 1.2 m wide or 15 m2 dropped, outline simplified 0.25 m.","limits":"Fronts are the survey's own lines (exact). The back of each body is read from the image: expect about +-5 m (image accuracy stated 5 m, measured 4.4 m mean against 13 roof corners on 6 Nov). Judged by eye on two crops only. Dark or grey roofs are missed, so some fronts stay open lines.","counts":{"front pieces with a body":794,"front length with a body m":3724,"joined bodies":221,"rings":242,"area m2":17267},"made":"13 Nov 2026, offline from the files above (not by a kit script)","rings":[[[31307.47,30526.04],[31305.85,30527.32],[31316.08,30540.27],[31317.7,30538.99]],[[31261.35,30566.35]